/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn4683view1\",\"pattern\":\"2025\"}); Total lines: 19\nL0: # Wenya Xie\nL1: \nL2: Ph.D. student @ UMN CSE · Reasoning · Agent memory · Long-horizon interaction\nL3: \nL4: cite0†Image: little_river.jpg L5: \nL6: I’m Wenya Xie, a Ph.D. student in Computer Science at the University of Minnesota (UMN), advised by cite1†Prof. Zirui Liu†zirui-ray-liu.github.io . Previously, I worked as a research assistant at CUHK (Shenzhen) with Prof. Benyou Wang and Feng Jiang. I received my bachelor’s degree from Wuhan University.\nL7: My research centers on large language models, spanning long-horizon tasks, reasoning, memory, and human–AI collaboration. Currently I focus on two directions:\nL8: \nL9: • Reasoning & overthinking — why reasoning models waste decoding budget and how they can reason more efficiently and proactively: cite2†Word Salad Chopper†arxiv.org (EMNLP 2025 Oral) and cite3†Reasoning While Asking†arxiv.org (ACL 2026).\nL10: • Memory management for LLM agents — how agents store, update, and retrieve information, for test-time adaptation (cite4†How Memory Management Impacts LLM Agents†arxiv.org , ACL 2026) and long-horizon personalization (cite5†DynamicMem ).\nL11: \nL12: I’m always excited to connect. Questions, ideas, and early-stage thoughts are all welcome. If you have anything you’d like to discuss, feel free to reach out!\nL13: ## cite6†news L14: \nL15: Jun 22, 2026  | We released a new memory benchmark! Check out our project website: cite5†DynamicMem .\nL16: Apr 07, 2026  | Two papers accepted to ACL 2026: cite4†Memory management for LLM agents†arxiv.org (Oral) and cite3†Proactive reasoning in large language models†arxiv.org L17: Sep 18, 2025  | One paper accepted to NeurIPS 2025 as an Oral Presentation: cite7†reproducible reasoning in FP32†arxiv.org .\nL18: Aug 20, 2025  | One paper accepted to EMNLP 2025 as an Oral Presentation: cite2†WordSaladChopper†arxiv.org .\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAriyan Hossain - Porfolio (https://ariyanhossain2208.github.io/)\nciteturn4684view7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn4683view2\",\"pattern\":\"Gender\"}); Total lines: 148\nL0: # Ariyan Hossain\nL1: \nL2: Lecturer, Computer Science & Engineering\nL3: BRAC University, Dhaka\nL4: NLP · Fairness · Responsible AI\nL5: \nL6: cite0†Image: Portrait of Ariyan Hossain [ PHOTO ]\nL7: \nL8: cite1†about cite2†news cite3†publications cite4†experience cite5†education cite6†projects cite7†talks cite8†awards L9: \nL10: ariyan.hossain2208@gmail.com\nL11: cite9†google scholar†scholar.google.com · cite10†github†github.com L12: cite11†linkedin†linkedin.com · cite12†faculty page†cse.sds.bracu.ac.bd L13: cite13†curriculum vitae (pdf) CV is not yet publicly available yet.\nL14: I want language technologies to be\nL15: [Button: [MASK]] for the people who use them, in every language they speak.\nL16: \nL17: (Go ahead, unmask it. My thesis was about what models put in that blank.)\nL18: I am a Lecturer in Computer Science and Engineering at cite14†BRAC University†www.bracu.ac.bd , where I also completed my B.Sc. in Computer Science and Engineering with university's Highest Distinction (GPA: 4.0/4.0). My research sits at the intersection of natural language processing (NLP) and fairness: I study how language models absorb, express, and transfer bias, and how we can measure and mitigate it.\nL19: My undergraduate thesis, supervised by cite15†Dr. Farig Sadeque†sites.google.com , introduced MALoR, a masked-token metric for quantifying gender bias in encoder models, and showed that counterfactual data augmentation can reduce measured bias by up to 95%.\nL20: \nL21: I am looking for PhD opportunities for Spring 2027 / Fall 2027 in trustworthy and fair NLP, human centered NLP, privacy and security in LLMs, and multilingual, low-resource language technology. If our interests overlap, I would be glad to hear from you.\nL22: ## News\nL23:   * Aug 2026 Two of my papers (first author and third author) have been accepted as main conference at EMNLP 2026.\nL24:   * Mar 2026 Two papers submitted to ARR (targeting EMNLP 2026): one on gender bias transfer in LLM-assisted student writing, one on benchmarking Bengali dialectal bias.\nL25:   * Dec 2025 Our paper on RAG techniques for Bengali standard-to-dialect translation is published at the BLP Workshop, IJCNLP–AACL 2025.\nL26:   * Nov 2025 My undergraduate thesis work on gender bias in encoder models is now on arXiv (cite16†2511.00519†arxiv.org ).\nL27: [Button: + show more]\nL28: ## Publications & Preprints\nL29: \nL30: Contaminated Collaboration: Measuring Gender Bias Transfer in LLM-Assisted Student Writing 2026\nL31: \nL32: Ariyan Hossain, K. K. Rabbi, Farig Sadeque, S. M. Taiabul Haque\nL33: \nL34: accepted Main Conference @ EMNLP 2026\nL35: \nL36: cite17†[arXiv:2606.15914]†arxiv.org L37: \nL38: Conducted the first controlled study (N=153) on gender stereotype propagation in LLM-assisted career essay writing. Demonstrated bias transfer using a fine-tuned agency classifier and a novel Stereotype Congruence Rate (SCR) metric.\nL39: Benchmarking Bengali Dialectal Bias: A Multi-Stage Framework Integrating RAG-Based Translation and Human-Augmented RLAIF 2026\nL40: \nL41: K. M. J. Sami, D. Sumit, Ariyan Hossain, Farig Sadeque\nL42: \nL43: accepted Main Conference @ EMNLP 2026\nL44: \nL45: cite18†[arXiv:2603.21359]†arxiv.org L46: Created a benchmark evaluating 19 LLMs on 4,000 gold-labeled questions across nine Bengali dialects using RAG-based translation. Proposed an RLAIF bias evaluation framework with Chain-of-Thought rubrics and introduced the Cultural Bias Score (CBS) metric for safety-critical assessment.\nL47: \nL48: A Comparative Analysis of RAG Techniques for Bengali Standard-to-Dialect Machine Translation Using LLMs 2025\nL49: \nL50: K. M. J. Sami, D. Sumit, Ariyan Hossain, Farig Sadeque\nL51: \nL52: published BLP Workshop @ IJCNLP–AACL 2025, ACL Anthology\nL53: cite19†[paper]†aclanthology.org L54: \nL55: Designed two RAG pipelines for standard-to-dialectal Bengali translation across six dialects using in-context learning. Improved translation accuracy by over 25% with sentence-pair RAG, enabling Llama-3.1-8B to outperform GPT-OSS-120B.\nL56: \nL57: Exploring and Mitigating Gender Bias in Encoder-Based Transformer Models 2025\nL58: \nL59: Ariyan Hossain, K. M. A. Hannan, R. Haque, N. T. Rafa, H. Musarrat, S. A. Dipu, Farig Sadeque\nL60: \nL61: preprint Undergraduate Thesis, BRAC University\nL62: cite16†[arXiv:2511.00519]†arxiv.org L63: \nL64: Proposed MALoR, a metric for quantifying gender bias in encoder-based models. Built a gender-balanced pretraining dataset with over 19,000 counterfactual sentence pairs using CDA, reducing gender bias by up to 95%.\nL65: \nL66: Identifying Framing Bias in Online Climate Change News Articles 2024 – 2025\nL67: \nL68: Ariyan Hossain, with Dr. Muhammad Nur Yanhaona\nL69: \nL70: Research Project, BRAC University\nL71: Built a climate change news dataset using expert annotation and GPT-4 synthetic augmentation for multi-class framing classification. Fine-tuned Longformer, BigBird, BERT, and LLaMA 3.1, applying QLoRA for memory-efficient PEFT.\nL72: ## Work Experience\nL73: \nL74: 2024 – present\nL75: \nL76: cite20†Image: BRAC University logo BU\nL77: ### Lecturer, Dept. of CSE, BRAC University\nL78: \nL79: Dhaka, Bangladesh\nL80: \nL81: I teach CSE220 (Data Structures), CSE221 (Algorithms), and CSE440 (Natural Language Processing) to 300+ undergraduate students each semester.\nL82: \nL83: Other services\nL84:   * Thesis Supervisor: Co-supervised and supervised 50+ students working on NLP undergraduate theses\nL85:   * Pre-Thesis I Panel Judge: Reviewed and provided feedback on initial thesis drafts of undergraduate teams\nL86:   * Final Thesis Defense Panel Judge: Reviewed and evaluated completed undergraduate research works\nL87:   * Course Advisor: Advised students on and approved undergraduate courses, and created course routines\nL88: \nL89: 2023 – 2024\nL90: \nL91: cite20†Image: BRAC University logo BU\nL92: ### Research Assistant, Dept. of CSE, BRAC University\nL93: \nL94: Dhaka, Bangladesh\nL95: \nL96: Full-time RA under Dr. Muhammad Nur Yanhaona on news framing classification with ML and NLP.\nL97: \nL98: 2022 – 2023\nL99: \nL100: cite20†Image: BRAC University logo BU\nL101: \nL102: ### Student Tutor (ST), Dept. of CSE, BRAC University\nL103: \nL104: Dhaka, Bangladesh\nL105: \nL106: Graded, lectured occasionally, and held up to 15 hours/week of student consultations.\nL107: \nL108: ## Education\nL109: \nL110: 2020 – 2023\nL111: \nL112: cite20†Image: BRAC University logo BU\nL113: ### B.Sc. in Computer Science and Engineering, BRAC University\nL114: \nL115: Dhaka, Bangladesh\nL116: \nL117: Grade: GPA 4.0/4.0 (Highest Distinction)\nL118: Thesis: Exploring and Mitigating Gender Bias in Transformer-based Language Models\nL119: Relevant Coursework: NLP, Neural Networks, Artificial Intelligence, Linear Algebra, Calculus\nL120: \nL121: 2017 – 2019\nL122: \nL123: cite21†Image: Cambridge Assessment International Education logo CIE\nL124: ### Cambridge O & A Levels, Sunnydale\nL125: \nL126: Dhaka, Bangladesh\nL127: \nL128: Award: Outstanding Cambridge Learner Award for World's Highest Mark (100%) in AS Level Mathematics\nL129: ## Selected Projects\nL130: cite22†NLP · Fairness BiasGuard: Explainable sexism detection in online texts Developed deep learning models (CNN, BiLSTM, and GRU) for sexist content detection in online text, with data preprocessing, embedding generation, and exploratory analysis.†github.com cite23†NLP Sentiment Analysis on IMDB Movie Reviews Built sentiment analysis models using Naive Bayes, Logistic Regression, and LSTM to classify movie reviews, comparing traditional machine learning and deep learning approaches.†github.com cite24†Computer Vision Image Classification with CNN Variants on CIFAR-10 Designed and trained CNN models with varying architectures, comparing activation functions, kernel sizes, filters, and strides to evaluate their impact on image classification performance.†github.com cite25†Machine Learning Wine Quality Prediction using Machine Learning Built wine quality prediction models using Random Forest, Logistic Regression, Naive Bayes, and SVM, with feature engineering, scaling, and feature importance analysis.†github.com cite26†IoT · Arduino DisasterGuard: Home Security System using Arduino and Sensors Developed an Arduino-based home security system using multiple sensors to detect earthquakes, gas leaks, smoke, and intrusions, with real-time SMS and buzzer alerts.†github.com cite27†Web Platform Pet Care: Veterinary and Adoption Services Platform Developed a pet care management system with modules for feeding, medication, grooming, cleaning, veterinary services, and adoption using HTML, CSS, JavaScript, PHP, and MySQL.†github.com L131: More on cite10†GitHub →†github.com L132: ## Talks\nL133: \nL134: May 2025\nL135: \nL136: ### Talking to Machines: The Power of Natural Language Processing\nL137: \nL138: IEEE Robotics and Automation Society, BRAC University\nL139: \nL140: Introduced NLP from how machines understand language to recent technologies including LLMs to 140+ undergraduate students cite28†[slides]†drive.google.com L141: ## Awards & Achievements\nL142:   * BRAC University Highest Distinction: Awarded Highest Distinction for achieving a CGPA of 3.80 or higher. Graduated with perfect 4.0/4.0 GPA.2023\nL143:   * BRAC University 100% Performance-Based Scholarship: Received 100% scholarship for maintaining CGPA of 4.0/4.0 throughout undergraduate studies.2020 – 2023\nL144:   * BRAC University Vice Chancellor’s List: Recognized on Vice Chancellor's List 10 times during Bachelor's for achieving a GPA of 3.90-4.00 in multiple semesters.2020 – 2023\nL145:   * Outstanding Cambridge Learner Award: Awarded World Highest Marks (100%) in AS Level Mathematics.2019\nL146:   * The Daily Star Award for A Level Outstanding Results: Recognized for achieving a minimum of 3 A's in A Level examinations.2019\nL147: © 2026 Ariyan Hossain · Dhaka, Bangladesh last updated: july 2026\n"
